<title>UK: GB Railways considers Australian rail bid.</title>
<headline>GB Railways considers Australian rail bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>GB Railways Group Plc on Wednesday said it was considering whether to bid for the passenger rail division of Australian National Railway.</p>
<p>The Australian government has invited the British group to proceed to the due diligence stage as one of the short listed parties interested in bidding, GB Railways said.</p>
<p>GB Railways was floated on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market in January. The company holds the franchise for Anglia Railways.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
